    "created_at": "2021-09-01T18:31:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-01T18:31:10Z",
    "body": "> Feel free to review it again though.\r\n\r\nPING's normal expectation is that doc authors will start by doing a self-analysis.  Even if there aren't issues, I expect the authors to make an argument for why.  In some cases that's obvious.  I'm not sure it is here.\r\n\r\nYou might find [RFC3552 Section 5](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3552#section-5) and/or [RFC6973](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6973) helpful.  I'm not sure how much the usual [TAG/PING questionnaire ](https://w3ctag.github.io/security-questionnaire/)will help in this case, but it's worth looking through.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
